---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import "../../../../styles/hermes-academy-app.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Hermes Connect Academy | Learner Access"
  description="Private Hermes Connect Academy access for enrollment, curriculum progress, evidence submissions and human-reviewed progression."
  robots="noindex,nofollow"
>
  <div class="academy-app-page">
    <SiteHeader activePath="/paths/academy/" />
    <main id="main-content" class="academy-app-shell">
      <nav class="academy-app-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/paths/academy/">Academy</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">Hermes Connect learner access</span>
      </nav>

      <section class="academy-app-hero">
        <article class="academy-app-card">
          <p class="academy-app-eyebrow">Hermes Connect · Academy workspace</p>
          <h1>One learner identity. One reviewed progression path.</h1>
          <p>Hermes Business Academy keeps enrollment, authenticated curriculum progress, learner evidence and human progression review inside the same Hermes identity/session system. Public program pages remain the source of curriculum descriptions.</p>
          <div class="academy-app-actions">
            <a class="academy-app-button primary" href="/services/hermes-connect/academy/auth/">Sign in or create learner account</a>
            <a class="academy-app-button" href="/services/hermes-connect/academy/dashboard/">Open learner dashboard</a>
            <a class="academy-app-button" href="/services/hermes-connect/academy/progression/">Open progression</a>
            <a class="academy-app-button" href="/services/hermes-connect/academy/submissions/">Evidence submissions</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <aside class="academy-app-card academy-app-dark">
          <span class="academy-app-status">Private learner workspace</span>
          <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Application ≠ enrollment ≠ completion.</h2>
          <p>Creating an account or choosing a program does not automatically approve admission. Lesson counts and accepted evidence do not automatically complete a program. Academy completion remains a separate human decision and does not guarantee employment, income, certification, clients, commercial entitlement, or live operational access.</p>
          <a class="academy-app-button" href="/academy/apply/">Open public application</a>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="academy-app-grid" aria-label="Academy programs and method">
        <article class="academy-app-panel">
          <p class="academy-app-eyebrow">Current public programs</p>
          <h2>Start from an approved curriculum source.</h2>
          <div class="academy-app-programs">
            <article class="academy-program-card">
              <span class="academy-app-status">Program 01</span>
              <h3>U.S. Logistics Operations</h3>
              <p>Dispatch foundations, carrier/broker communication, equipment and lane logic, documents, negotiation practice and operating rhythm.</p>
              <a class="academy-app-button" href="/academy/us-logistics-operations/">Review curriculum</a>
            </article>
            <article class="academy-program-card">
              <span class="academy-app-status">Program 02</span>
              <h3>Marketing</h3>
              <p>Positioning, website-first content, channel distribution, lead journey, sales follow-up, analytics and improvement.</p>
              <a class="academy-app-button" href="/academy/marketing/">Review curriculum</a>
            </article>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="academy-app-panel">
          <p class="academy-app-eyebrow">Learning method</p>
          <h2>Progress remains evidence-led and human-reviewed.</h2>
          <p>The current Academy workflow moves through readiness, authenticated lessons, self-tracked lesson progress, evidence submission, reviewer feedback/correction and a separate human progression decision.</p>
          <div class="academy-app-note">A1 provides shared learner identity and enrollment. A2 provides authenticated curriculum and self-tracked lesson progress. A3 adds private evidence plus manually authorized review. A4 adds program-level human progression. Commercial access remains a separate A5 gate and is not inferred from any learner or reviewer state.</div>
          <div class="academy-app-actions">
            <a class="academy-app-button" href="/academy/how-training-works/">How training works</a>
            <a class="academy-app-button" href="/academy/resources/">Academy resources</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="academy-app-panel" style="margin-top:18px" aria-label="Authorized reviewer workspaces">
        <p class="academy-app-eyebrow">Manually authorized reviewers only</p>
        <h2>Reviewer workspaces stay behind the separate Academy allowlist.</h2>
        <p>A valid Hermes account alone does not grant reviewer power. These routes require an active <code>academy_reviewer_access</code> authorization and continue to enforce program scope and self-review restrictions.</p>
        <div class="academy-app-actions">
          <a class="academy-app-button" href="/services/hermes-connect/academy/reviewer/">Evidence review queue</a>
          <a class="academy-app-button" href="/services/hermes-connect/academy/reviewer/progression/">Progression review queue</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
